          "why_it_matters": "Punch Brothers are most interesting when virtuosity stops sounding like a demonstration and becomes ensemble grammar. The current quintet puts Thile's mandolin, Pikelny's banjo, Eldridge's guitar, Kowert's bass and Haas's fiddle inside music that can move from string-band pulse to chamber precision and progressive structure without changing personnel. The new all-instrumental record makes that interaction — rather than lyrics or a front-person narrative — the clearest reason to hear this tour.",
